  "identifiability_text": "The model has three unidentifiable parameters per site: λ (leakage fraction), Q (stream flow), and τ (travel time). These are drawn from prior distributions informed by published sewer-leakage studies and OSM stream geometry. The sensitivity analysis (Spearman ρ) identifies which prior dominates the score uncertainty at each site. Parameters informed by measured data (DDD, fe, PNEC, LOD) reduce uncertainty only when sourced. With illustrative parameters (D33), the model demonstrates the pipeline mechanism only — scores are not evidence of actual risk.",
